      "description": "LifeWorks provides housing and case management specifically for youth and young adults (generally 16–26) experiencing or at risk of homelessness, including those currently in or aging out of Texas foster care. Programs include fully subsidized apartments (up to 18 months), step‑down rental assistance (up to 2 years), The Works affordable apartments, and After Care Transitional Services (ACTS) for ages 17½–20 who are in or aged out of foster care in DFPS Region 7 (includes Travis County). They can also complete the Coordinated Assessment for the local homelessness system.",
